+  `sha256:nFd97--oj5PkYjdpN45r3IQcojKSjaY2B3hvehY9vXc`, posted
+  2026-11-22T16:47:03Z (verified present exactly once on the board).
+- Scope: NO theorem completion for S(n)/SORT-BOUND-U; no repo/Lean/test/CI/
+  ledger/canonical-main/bill/ballot change. External writes are this record and
+  the single #301 comment above.
+
+## Verdict: ACCEPT
+
+A rigorous, correctly scoped, purely deductive result. It refutes the
+"FF_n information-tight for all n" horn and closes the all-n FF-tightness
+question that the `endpoint-vs-free-pair-gap-alln` bounded commission
+(n=5..9) explicitly left open. Not a new lower bound on S(n), not a
+complexity-class placement.
+
+## Independently verified evidence
+
+1. Core theorem re-derived from scratch. FF_n = two disjoint 2-chains +
+   (n-4) free keys, e(FF_n) = n!/4. Strategy: compare keys 0,1 (c1), then
+   keys 2,3 (c2); every outcome gives a poset isomorphic to FF_n (the pairs
+   are disjoint). Continue with an optimal height-F(FF_n) strategy. Every
+   permutation is sorted in <= 2+F(FF_n) comparisons, so S(n) <= 2+F(FF_n),
+   i.e. F(FF_n) >= S(n)-2. Strategy-composition (minimax) argument; inequality
+   direction correct.
+2. Information shift: ceil(log2(m/4)) = ceil(log2 m) - 2 for integer m, so
+   ceil(log2 e(FF_n)) = ceil(log2 n!) - 2. Hence
+   d(FF_n) = F(FF_n) - ceil(log2(n!/4)) >= S(n) - ceil(log2 n!) = excess_S(n),
+   for all n >= 4.
+3. n=12 arithmetic rechecked: 12! = 479001600 (ceil log2 = 29);
+   12!/4 = 119750400 (ceil log2 = 27). S(12)=30 is a documented literature
+   fact (Wells 1965/66; Peczarski 2012; Stober-Weiss 2023), confirmed in the
+   SoringP1 main checkout at docs/research-plan.md:17,
+   docs/research-n12-nontightness.md:12,
+   docs/research-hardness-boundaries.md:50, docs/literature.md:12.
+   Therefore F(FF_12) >= 28 > 27, d(FF_12) >= 1 > 0. FF_12 is reachable at
+   depth 2 from the antichain; n=12 is minimal since S(n)=ceil(log2 n!) for
+   n<=11.
+4. Small-n corroboration independently re-executed by running the reporter's
+   scratch solver (/tmp/opencode/ff_solver.py): n=4,5,6 give S=5,7,10 and
+   F(FF)=3,5,8 = S-2, zero excess. The deductive theorem does not depend on
+   any computation; n>=8 exact FF search is infeasible and not claimed.
+
+## Honest limits confirmed
+
+- Finite witness n=12 refutes "tight for all n"; it does NOT establish
+  infinitely many positive-excess n (that needs excess_S(n)>0 infinitely
+  often, which is open; Sergeev gives only an o(n) upper surplus).
+- Derived from known S(12)=30, so no new lower bound.
+- No P/NP/coNP placement; SORT-BOUND-U stays in PSPACE with the same
+  sparsity/Mahaney and winning-frontier barriers; certificate completeness
+  at height S(n) untouched; no general-poset hardness transfers.
+
+## Next (recorded, not claimed): can a single positive excess at a reachable
+depth-two state be amplified to an infinite family, or is tightness-density-zero
+the truth? Genuinely open; left to independent future work.
+
+S(n)/SORT-BOUND-U remain OPEN.
